    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60548" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῡδῐ-άνειρα</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰν], ἡ, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῦδος</span>) fem.Adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bringing men glory</i> or
				<i>renown</i>, Homeric epith. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχη</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.225
			</span></i>, al.; once of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγορή</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				1.490
			</span></i>; of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φύσις</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>H.</u>
				10.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>glorified by men, famous for men</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σπάρτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>APl.</u>
					1.1
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Damag.
			</span></i>).</div>
